  "command": "source 'scripts/env.sh' && CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_COMPOSER='/usr/bin/composer' LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_MAX_LOAD='8' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_MODES='result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_OUTPUT='build/nominal-primitive-subtype-php-promotion/ordinary-result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_PHP_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_PHP_COMPOSER_VERSION='2.5.5' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_PHP_VERSION='8.2.33' LEAN_BRIDGE_PHP='/usr/bin/php' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' 'node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' '--test-name-pattern=^installed primitive-base nominal PHP packages reproduce and relocate ordinary result-only$' 'tests/helpers/nominal-primitive-subtype-php-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Composer ZIP. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation; unchanged weak and strict callers replay after moving the installed tree, giving four executions per selection. The standalone result-only API projects all nineteen primitive payloads through scalars, copied containers, records, variants and aliases without any input constructor selections. Primitive-base nominal native PHP acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, nested Pair/Array/Option/Except values, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete Composer ZIPs from two author roots, remove author and build roots, install offline, and replay weak and strict PHP callers before and after relocation. The runs use PHP 8.2.33 and Composer 2.5.5 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, 64-bit machine words and an 8.0 host-load admission ceiling. Original packages, receipts, Composer inputs, execution records and selected sources are retained; external toolchain binaries are represented by version, size and digest. PHP consumer source remains required at runtime. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. Hosted release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the recurring workflow; archived absolute paths describe the original local runs and are not CI prerequisites.",
